{
  "title": "Congenital Hallux Varus (Atavistic Great Toe)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4076/congenital-hallux-varus-atavistic-great-toe",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 1 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Congenital Hallux Varus, also known as Atavistic Great Toe, is a rare idiopathic condition caused by a firm, band-like abductor hallucis muscle that occurs in children after walking age and presents with varus deformity of the big toe.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with varus deformity of the first toe with radiographs showing a short, thick 1st metatarsal.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually operative with abductor hallucis muscle release for mild resistant cases or excision of the central portion of epiphyseal bracket in cases with a bracket causing the deformity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "presents in children after walking age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "longitudinal epiphyseal bracket of the first metatarsal or proximal phalanx",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "deformity at metatarsophalangeal joint due to",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "imbalance between the great toe abductor and adductors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "firm, fibrous, band-like **abductor hallucis muscle**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "short, thick first metatarsal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "longitudinal bracket epiphysis of the 1st metatarsal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "underlying skeletal dysplasia (diastrophic dwarfism)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "do not confuse with metatarus primus varus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "varus deformity of the 1st metatarsal (no deformity at MTP joint)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Associated conditions**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often associated with **polydactyly**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cosmetic deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "difficult to put on shoes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "usually painless",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Deformity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can vary in severity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "few degrees to 90 degress",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views of the foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "oblique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "short, thick 1st metatarsal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4076/images/chv.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Must be differentiated from metatarsus adductus",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation alone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "rare as deformity is thought to worsen with age",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "surgical correction often proposed in infancy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "abductor hallucis muscle release",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mild and resistant deformities",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "excision of central portion of epiphyseal bracket",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if epiphyseal bracket found to be the cause of Hallux Varus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "resumption of longitudinal growth common if performed at a young age",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "secondary corrective realignment or lengthening is sometimes needed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Farmer technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4076/images/f029-018-9780323374620.jpg",
                  "caption": "Farmer technique"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indication",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "moderate to severe deformities",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique creates syndactyly between the 2nd toe and hallux",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "maintains deformity correction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence** of deformity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Incomplete correction** of deformity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
